# One line ending, LF. The tree lives on one Fedora machine (2026-09-22); it was once edited
# from Windows too, and this is what kept that from flipping files back and forth.
* text=auto
# The tool writes LF; with core.autocrlf the checkout wrote CRLF, so every tool write
# flipped a whole file's line endings and git warned on each one. One ending, everywhere.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.ino text eol=lf
*.pdf binary
*.STEP binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
